    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0135" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg101"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2734.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my dispatch No. 2705, of March 11 last,
                    I informed you that I had applied to the Tsung-li Yamên to order the dismissal
                    of the magistrate, Liu Yan-Kwang, from office on account of neglect of duty
                    during the riot at Kiang Yin, which occurred last summer during my absence in
                    Japan.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose a translation of a communication from the Yamên, from
                    which it appears that this magistrate has been dismissed from his office.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d98-a1.xml" xpointer="d98-a1"/>
            </div>
